    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, labelled by the calendar year it ends in, e.g. `FY26`).\n\n**New cohesive unit** \u2014 `FiscalYear.java`: a small helper owning the single 1-July rule, with `of(date)` (fiscal-year number) and `label(date)` (`FY<YY>`). This keeps the rule in one place so every call site stays a one-line change.\n\n**Wired it in with minimal, simple edits:**\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` response mapping and switched the `membershipNumber` year segment from `registrationDate.getYear()` to `FiscalYear.of(...)`.\n- `LogAuditOnCreate.java` \u2014 same year-segment switch for the audited membership number, keeping it consistent with the DTO.\n- `TenureFactor.java` \u2014 tenure now qualifies on elapsed fiscal years (`FiscalYear.of(now) - FiscalYear.of(registered) >= 1`) instead of a 365-day window.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` property and updated the `membershipNumber` / `membershipPoints` descriptions to match.\n\nThe registration date fed to `FiscalYear` is the one already business-day-adjusted in `BuildOwner`, so `fiscalYear`, the membership number, and tenure all derive from the same adjusted date. Structural impact stayed low: each changed function remained trivial (CC ~1), and the shared logic lives in one new small class rather than being duplicated or bloating an existing one.",
